<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Owain Glyndŵr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1359–c. 1415</span> · Also known as Owain Glyndwr, Owen Glendower</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Owain Glyndŵr was a Welsh landowner descended from the princes of Powys who was proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> in 1400 and led the last great revolt against English rule. He held parliaments at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/machynlleth">Machynlleth</a>, sought French help and planned a Welsh church and universities. By 1409 his strongholds had fallen, and he disappeared around 1415.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/owain-glyndwr.jpg" alt="Owain Glyndŵr" width="320" height="477" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jr8825 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Owain_Glynd%C5%B5r_portrait.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
